{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance Annual General Adjustment 5% cap (Measure BB)","requirement":"The Annual General Adjustment capping yearly rent increases for fully covered units may not exceed 5%. Landlords may still exceed 5% using banked unused AGAs up to the rent ceiling; capital improvement increases require completed work.","key_value":"5% annual cap (AGA)","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units have a rent ceiling limiting increases to the Annual General Adjustment. Multifamily units built before 1980 are fully covered; new construction with a certificate of occupancy after 1980 is only partially covered.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1980","basis":"certificate_of_occupancy"}],"per_tenancy":"A unit where the tenant shares kitchen or bath with the landlord is exempt only if the landlord lived on the same property when the tenancy started.","coverage_quotes":["Units that are fully covered will have a rent ceiling, meaning rent increases will be limited by the Annual General Adjustment set by the Rent Board each year.","New Construction Units (units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980)","Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy."]},"exemptions":"New construction units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980, most single-family homes and most condominiums are only partially covered (no rent ceiling). Shared kitchen/bath units are exempt only if the landlord lived on the property.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-11","valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Federal, state or administrative law prohibits rent control for certain subsidized unit types, so those units are only partially covered.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance just cause eviction changes (Measure BB)","requirement":"Tenants in covered units may be evicted only with just cause. Nonpayment eviction requires debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent; tenants cannot be evicted for refusing to sign a substantially similar lease; lease-breach notices must describe the breach and harm.","key_value":"rental debt ≥ 1 month's Fair Market Rent","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance cannot be evicted without just cause. Government-owned or -subsidized units are now fully or partially covered.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"A unit where the tenant shares kitchen or bath with the landlord is exempt only if the landlord lived on the same property when the tenancy started.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-11","valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","n_rules":2,"note":null}

